steps.text:
[HIIT](g:hiit) is a run of hard [work intervals](g:work-interval) split by easier [relief intervals](g:relief-interval). Buchheit and Laursen list up to **nine variables** a coach can set [[c:nine-variables]]:

- work interval: intensity and duration;
- relief interval: intensity and duration;
- the type of exercise (flat running, uphill, cycling…);
- number of reps and number of series;
- recovery between series: duration and intensity.

Change any one and the session's effect on the body changes. So '4 × 4 min' is not a full prescription: how hard, with what recovery?

Two quick sums describe a session: the total **work time** (series × reps × work duration) and the **work:rest ratio** (30 s on, 15 s off is 2:1).
